      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Personally I linked my meta account to my regular account, so when I do run on quest and just choose the right hand option and then I'm logged in as myself.\n\nWould be nice to have less trouble with logging in with VRChat account for the times I need to use an alt to test certain things",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-01-14T20:59:43.166Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "My password is many random characters.\n\nThe Quest raycast laser based keyboard input is INCREDIBLY awkward to input this, not to mention the fact that I haven't memorized it yet, so I have to peek under the headset, hoping it doesn't go to sleep and close VRC, to get every few characters read out to input them into the headset.\n\nIf the Quest client simply remembered the password between versions so when I (rarely) go back to Quest mode to test a world I don't have to do this, it would be MUCH more sensible.\n\nI have 2FA anyway, so there's very little reason to not remember the password...\n\nThanks for reading / considering my feature request!",
